member.param:
Specifies the quality of the encoded image, when using a lossy compression format:
            the value of 1 specifies the maximum possible quality, resulting in minimum compression;
            the value of 0 specifies the minimum possible quality, resulting in maximum compression.

Specifies the quality of the encoded image, when using a lossy compression format:
            the value of 1 specifies the maximum possible quality, resulting in minimum compression;
            the value of 0 specifies the minimum possible quality, resulting in maximum compression.

Specifies the maximum desired size of the image to save:
            if the image is larger than the specified size, it is downscaled to fit that size;
            if the image is smaller than the specified size, it is saved with its original size.

Specifies the quality of the encoded image, when using a lossy compression format:
            the value of 1 specifies the maximum possible quality, resulting in minimum compression;
            the value of 0 specifies the minimum possible quality, resulting in maximum compression.

Specifies a scale factor, which can be used to reduce the size of the final image:
            values below 1 downscale the image before saving, thus reducing the final image size;
            values above 1 upscale the image before saving, thus increasing the final image size.

member.summary:
Gets or sets the quality of the encoded image, when using a lossy compression format:
the value of 1 specifies the maximum possible quality, resulting in minimum compression;
the value of 0 specifies the minimum possible quality, resulting in maximum compression.

Gets or sets a scale factor, which can be used to reduce the size of the final image:
values below 1 downscale the image before saving, thus reducing the final image size;
values above 1 upscale the image before saving, thus increasing the final image size.

